<h3>FAQ</h3>
<hr />
<br />

<div class="table-info">
    <p>
        <h5>What is Massage Therapy?</h5>

        Massage therapy is a clinically-oriented healthcare option that involves the hands-on manipulation of the body's soft tissues, 
        <br />
        including muscles, connective tissue, tendons, ligaments, and joints. It is an evidence-based practice used to develop, maintain, 
        <br />
        or rehabilitate physical function, as well as to relieve pain and manage stress.
    </p>
    <hr />
    <p>
        <h5>This is my first massage, what should I expect?</h5>
    
        You should expect your RMT to have a brief conversation with you pertaining to your health and wellness prior to your massage. 
        <br />
        They may conduct a few brief assessments to determine the location and type of injury or condition you may be experiencing.
        <br />
        During your treatment, you will have the areas that you specified worked on, and your RMT will ensure throughout your treatment that you
        <br />
        are comfortable and that the pressure is adequate for your needs and comfort level. After your session, it is typical that your RMT will 
        <br />
        discuss their findings, and advise on specific stretches or exercises that may help you.
    </p>
    <hr />
    <p>
        <h5>How will massage therapy benefit me?</h5>
       
        With professional registered massage therapy, you can experience relief from muscular tension and pain, receive increased range of 
        <br />
        motion and a reduction of mental stress levels. Massage is a natural healing process that can deliver both physical and emotional benefits.
        <br />
        Treatments are specifically tailored to meet your needs. Your RMT will take the time to read over your health history and discuss your concerns 
        <br />
        before commencing your treatment.
    </p>
</div>



